From 2ff581b233a161a5cfb9b07813003ad72391801e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild Idler Patch <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 06:10:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Rooftail (Red Panda) idle blink-out bug, extend pipeline
 to support mixed sheet+override sources

- Root cause: the sheet's idle row's last 2 of 8 frames were fully
  zero-opacity blank (confirmed by inspecting the actual alpha channel),
  causing the loop to play 6 real frames then 2 invisible ones before
  jumping back to frame 0 -- read as 'blinks out, then reappears.'
- Fixed with a corrected, already-trimmed 6-frame replacement file for
  idle specifically; idle2/movement/sleep stay on the original sheet.
- This needed a genuine capability the pipeline didn't have: PetSpec's
  two source shapes (sheet_file+rows vs. anim_files) were strictly
  either/or. Extended import_pets.py's main() to merge both into the
  same per-animation dict before the shared trim/recolor step, with
  anim_files winning on a name collision.

Verified thoroughly given this touched shared pipeline code: re-ran the
refactored script against every species I had real source art for (5
dogs, Ashwing's replacement files) plus a synthetic stand-in sheet for
Rooftail specifically built to exercise the new merge path, confirming
zero behavior change for every prior single-source spec and correct
output for the new mixed case (idle: 6 frames from the override,
idle2/movement/sleep: 8 frames each still from the sheet, sampled
pixels confirming idle2 still recolors correctly). Full tsc --noEmit
and vite build pass clean.

Art itself is gitignored same as every other species -- regenerate via
'python3 tools/import_pets.py --src <folder with
Red_Panda_Sprite_Sheet.png and Red-Panda-idle-fixed.png> --out
public/pets --only rooftail'.
